# UX/UI construction (not a review-only doc)

When adding or changing UI, **implement** [`docs/ux-ui-guidelines.md`](../../docs/ux-ui-guidelines.md). Tokens, Settings-only chrome, and no-raw-hex: [`docs/DESIGN_GUIDE.md`](../../docs/DESIGN_GUIDE.md) and `design-system.mdc`. `/ux-review` uses this same law; it is not a second checklist.

## Must do in the same slice

- Users know where they are, what they can do, and what happens next
- One primary button per view; secondary quieter; destructive separate
- Visible labels (placeholder is not the label); copy in i18n (`t()` / `stringResource`)
- Empty, error, and loading states with a named next action (honest empty, not fake data)
- Keyboard + visible focus ring (never `outline: none` without a replacement)
- Touch targets ≥ 44px; icon-only controls have accessible names
- Existing tokens/components only — no new visual system, no AI-slop art, no raw hex
- Accessibility is not optional polish (WCAG 2.2 AA)
- Toasts confirm; errors stay in-place. No stacked modals. No blocking the app for a local save

## Gaps

If you cannot fix a violation in this slice, append a `UX-NNN` item to the BUILD_PLAN UX inventory **now** (status `planned` only — never backlog/deferred/later). `/build` does not auto-drain inventory; `/ux-apply UX-NNN` implements one item.
